    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Ad_Magazine_Newspaper_Print</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Ad - Magazine/ Newspaper_(Print)</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to place an ad in Magazine/Newspaper. The ad shall feature &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices, with the correct Intel processor logos (Exhibit A), processor mentions with appropriate trademarks (®/™) and pre-approved Intel messaging as agreed between Retailer and the Intel Account Manager.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Collateral_Print</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Collateral_(Print)</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to implement and maintain an  on retailer.com. The page content shall be provided or pre-approved by Intel, featuring &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices with the correct Intel processor logos (Exhibit A), processor mentions with appropriate trademarks (®/™) and pre-approved Intel messaging as agreed between Retailer and the Intel Account Manager.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_EPOS_with_intel_Content</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_EPOS_with_intel_Content</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to display and administer Intel content in ePOS across 100 stores. The ePOS shall run on at least   of the &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices in each store throughout the duration of the store opening hours, including the correct Intel processor logos (Exhibit A), Intel processor mentions with appropriate trademarks (®/™) and pre-approved Intel messaging as agreed between retailer and the Intel Account Manager. The ePOS shall also be visible on the full screen of each Intel-based device and not be covered by any software pop-ups.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_End_Cap</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_End-Cap</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to display and administer end-cap locations across # stores, each displaying at least # &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; device. The end-cap backdrop display shall not be covered with any additional promotional/pricing information.Retailer shall run the activity as described until the end of the Timeframe. If any conditions stated above are not met, Intel reserves the right to reduce the amounts payable for the activity.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Headcount</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Headcount</shortDescription>
        <value>MDF Recipient hires individual(s) whose principal job responsibility is to promote Intel-based systems, products and/or technologies. The intent of this activity is to provide headcount to support Intel-specific sales, marketing and/or training-focused activities.  Administrative and management costs such as the cost of filing claims are excluded.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_IPOS</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_IPOS</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to display and administer the latest version of the Intel iPOS (as provided by Intel to the retailer) across 100 stores. The Intel iPOS shall run on at least 50%  of the &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices in each store throughout the duration of the store opening hours. The Intel iPOS shall also be visible on the full screen of each Intel-based device and not be covered by any software pop-ups.

These requirements do not apply to Intel-based devices which are included in a separate ‘shop environment’ zone in store which is fully funded by a third party original equipment manufacturer.

Retailer shall run the activity as described until the end of the Timeframe. If any conditions stated above are not met, Intel reserves the right to reduce the amounts payable for the activity.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Intel_POS_Materials</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Intel_POS_Materials</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to display and administer Intel-approved posters across # stores. The posters shall prominently promote the features and benefits of &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices, products and/or technologies, including the correct Intel processor logos (Exhibit A), processor mentions with appropriate trademarks (®/™) and pre-approved Intel messaging as agreed between retailer and the Intel Account Manager.

Retailer shall run the activity as described until the end of the Timeframe. If any conditions stated above are not met, Intel reserves the right to reduce the amounts payable for the activity.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Newsletter_PC_Products</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Newsletter - PC_Products</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to send out a Newsletter to its owned database or lawfully bought distribution list. The Newsletter   and shall feature &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices in a prominent position, including the correct Intel processor logos (Exhibit A), processor mentions with appropriate trademarks (®/™) and pre-approved Intel messaging as agreed between Retailer and the Intel Account Manager. The Newsletter shall link to the appropriate Intel landing page or product page on retailer.com. Retailer shall run the activity as described until reaching either (a) the agreed Newsletter Circulation, or (b) the agreed conversions to the site. If any conditions stated above are not met, Intel reserves the right to reduce the amounts payable for the activity.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_RSP_Training_F2F</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_RSP_Training - F2F</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to allow an Intel representative to train at least 100 RSPs of its sales force on the features and benefits of &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices. The session shall take place  of the retailer’s premises with at least 1 hour dedicated to the Intel training. The training materials will be provided or pre-approved by Intel.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_RSP_Training_IREP</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_RSP_Training - IREP</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to have at least 100 RSPs of its sales force undertake and pass at least three of the Intel iREP training Modules including one 10th Gen focused module (on retailedge.intel.com), as agreed between retailer and the Intel Account Manager.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Riser</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Riser</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to display and administer Intel-branded risers underneath &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices across # stores. There shall be at least # risers deployed per store, each including the correct Intel processor logos (Exhibit A), trademarks (®/™) and pre-approved Intel messaging as agreed between retailer and the Intel Account Manager.
Each riser provided by Intel remains the property of Intel. Changes to the riser (including changes to paper insert or addition of retailer branding) need written approval by Intel Account Manager. Any riser not provided by Intel must follow the same guidelines and be approved before deployment to be eligible.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Store_Zone</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_Store_Zone</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to refurbish or change existing store zones across [#] stores. The zones shall be clearly dedicated as &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; areas and be located within, adjacent to or in front of the PC department, featuring each at least [#] &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices from more than one OEM.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_TV_Ad_in_store</fullName>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Core_MDF_Sales_Readiness_TV_Ad - in_store</shortDescription>
        <value>Retailer to install and play a video ad on all TV screens from the TV area across 100 stores (around 1000 screens in total). The video shall last 60 seconds with at least 30 seconds dedicated to feature &lt;Intel-based focus&gt; devices, including the correct Intel processor logos (Exhibit A), processor mentions with appropriate trademarks (®/™), full Intel audio Sig ID and pre-approved Intel messaging as agreed between Retailer and the Intel Account Manager.</value>
    </labels>
